abstract: >
  The increase of GNSS observations worldwide creates new opportunities for large-scale analysis,
  but also introduces challenges in data holdings, retrieval, and quality control. In this frame,
  this open-source Python package, GRINQ, automates these steps through a unified workflow for
  retrieving RINEX data across multiple data repositories and computing quality statistics. A
  dedicated mirroring functionality enables the cloning of selected data, allowing users to maintain
  synchronized copies of remote repositories, facilitating the subsequent analysis of RINEX data.
